From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 07:47:39 -0400
Subject: stop tab favicons tiling in their slot

The 18 DIP favicon slot drew a 16 DIP bitmap with a source rect of the slot's
size, and gfx::Canvas fills source/destination mismatches with
SkTileMode::kRepeat -- so the icon's edge pixels repeated into the extra two
pixels and favicons looked doubled. Both draw sites now use the image's own
size as the source rect, which scales instead of tiling.

Why: reported from real use as "favicons repeat themselves", and no screenshot
of a fresh profile showed it because default favicons are already 16.
Removable when: favicons are requested at the slot's size instead of 16.
---
 chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab/tab_icon.cc | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab/tab_icon.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab/tab_icon.cc
index 16dfe52640415..8f96070edffd8 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab/tab_icon.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/tab/tab_icon.cc
@@ -350,7 +350,7 @@ void TabIcon::PaintAttentionIndicatorAndIcon(gfx::Canvas* canvas,
   // . a circle in the bottom right (or left in rtl) of the favicon.
   if (!icon.isNull()) {
     canvas->SaveLayerAlpha(0xff);
-    canvas->DrawImageInt(icon, 0, 0, bounds.width(), bounds.height(),
+    canvas->DrawImageInt(icon, 0, 0, icon.width(), icon.height(),
                          bounds.x(), bounds.y(), bounds.width(),
                          bounds.height(), false);
     cc::PaintFlags clear_flags;
@@ -490,7 +490,7 @@ void TabIcon::MaybePaintFavicon(gfx::Canvas* canvas,
     canvas->Translate(gfx::Vector2d(-bounds.x(), -bounds.y()));
   }
 
-  canvas->DrawImageInt(icon, 0, 0, bounds.width(), bounds.height(), bounds.x(),
+  canvas->DrawImageInt(icon, 0, 0, icon.width(), icon.height(), bounds.x(),
                        bounds.y(), bounds.width(), bounds.height(),
                        /*filter=*/true);
 
